{#
  The shell the pages of this subsystem share: the head, the bar at the top and
  the frame. There are two pages — the configuration as it is, and the prices to
  be written — and the shell is here so that the second one is not a copy of the
  first that drifts from it.

  It is its own shell, not `commons/base.njk`: the shared one asks for the
  language and the translation of a page of the product, and this is internal
  instrumentation, whose labels are system terms and stay in English like the rest
  of what is internal. See README.md, "Why not the shared shell".

  Blocks: `title`, `nav`, `content`, `footer`.
  Expected: view.readAt.
#}<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{% block title %}configuration — webtools{% endblock %}</title>
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css">
</head>
<body>

<header class="top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="brand">webtools <span>configurator</span></span>
    <span class="read-at">read at {{ view.readAt }}</span>
  </div>
</header>

{% block nav %}{% endblock %}

<main class="wrap">
{% block content %}{% endblock %}

  <footer>
{% block footer %}{% endblock %}
  </footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
